Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 01:33:47 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 187/206] refactor: strip the flicker-hunt debug
 instrumentation from Cry3DEngine

The per-object cull logging, submission diff recorder and the four
atomic counters were battlefield instrumentation for the RSM caster
stability investigation (case closed in 07_flicker_case_file.md). All
of it lives in shared engine files, so removing it shrinks the diff a
future community-version merge has to carry. The functional pieces stay:
volume-overlap RSM membership, the fixed traversal-marking bit, the
stable-caster type filter and the FMBIT 64-bit mask fixes. r_LPVDebug
modes 2/3 keep their shader-side visualizations, only the 3DEngine log
output is gone (recoverable from git history if ever needed again).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tu9cj9ax1mqCV93HVfCfpW
